  "problem": "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $6\\,|\\,x$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $3\\,|\\,x$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\nI. $6\\,|\\,x$ is sufficient for $3\\,|\\,x$\n\nII. For $3\\,|\\,x,$ it is sufficient that $6\\,|\\,x$\n\nIII. $6\\,|\\,x$ is necessary for $3\\,|\\,x$\n\nIV. For $6\\,|\\,x,$ it is necessary that $3\\,|\\,x$",
